hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1118","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Yazid bin Kaysan narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We had a wedding with The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and we did not wake up until the sun had risen. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let every person take his head.” His mount, for this is a place where Satan has come to us.” So we did so, so he called for water and performed ablution, then he prayed two prostrations when the prayer was established, and he prayed. In the morning"
